# CS536 project (always on)

This repo is the CS536 / ML II research project **Learning to Select Context per Code Diff: An Accuracy-Cost Trade-off for LLM Code Review**.

On every task, on any platform:

1. Follow root `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/skills/cs536-project/SKILL.md`.
2. Before acting, recursively list `docs/` and read **every document in full**,
   including PDFs, DOCX files, Markdown, and future additions. This applies to
   setup, coding, debugging, notebooks, reviews, experiments, and writing.
3. Use `.cursor/skills/cs536-project/docs-index.md` only as a navigation aid.
   Report unreadable documents explicitly after trying extraction/rendering tools.
4. Surface conflicts and distinguish historical notes from current decisions.
   Follow explicit current user instructions; otherwise prefer current official
   course/instructor guidance and the latest applicable project decisions.
5. Re-list `docs/` for each new task/session and read new or changed documents.
   Reuse full reads only within the same active session while files are unchanged.
   Include this requirement when handing work to another agent.
